## Summary
Two fixes to the photo viewer on photo cases (`web/src/components/case/PhotoStage.tsx`):

**1. The picture can't be dragged out of the frame.** Before, dragging moved the photo anywhere, even fully off-screen, leaving a black frame. Every pan and zoom now goes through a `clamp` step:
- Where the picture fits the frame on an axis, it is centred and can't be dragged along that axis. At "fit" it doesn't move at all.
- When zoomed in, you can pan around, but it stops at the picture's edges.
- No zooming out below "fit", which only added black around the picture. On small images "1:1" no longer shrinks the picture below fit.
- The view is re-clamped when the frame resizes.
- The grab cursor only shows when there is something to pan.

**2. Scrolling over the picture zooms it without scrolling the page.**
- React's `onWheel` listener is passive, so its `preventDefault()` was ignored and the page scrolled while zooming. It is now a native listener with `passive: false`, and `.photo-canvas` gets `overscroll-behavior: contain`.
- Zoom now follows the scroll distance instead of 1.2× per event. A mouse notch is still about 1.2×; a trackpad's stream of tiny events zooms smoothly instead of racing. Line and page scroll units are converted to pixels, and trackpad pinch (ctrl+wheel) zooms too.

The region selection for enhancing (`Z`), the loupe (`M`), overlays and finding boxes are unchanged. Zoom by keys, double-click or clicking a flagged region goes through the same clamp.

## Testing
I drove a photo case (a 24 MP JPEG) in headless browsers and measured where the picture ends up and the page's scroll position.

**Chrome:**
| Action | Result |
|---|---|
| Drag at fit | Picture doesn't move |
| Zoom out ×10 | Stops at fit, centred |
| Zoom in, then drag far down-right and up-left | Stops exactly at the picture's edges, no black gap |
| Narrow the window to 700 px | Picture stays in frame |
| Wheel over the picture | Zooms; page `scrollY` unchanged |
| Wheel outside the picture | Page scrolls normally |

**Firefox 159** (WebDriver BiDi):
| Action over the picture | Picture width | Page `scrollY` |
|---|---|---|
| Trackpad-sized scroll up (30 small steps) | 898 → 1242 px, smooth | unchanged |
| Trackpad-sized scroll down | back to fit | unchanged |
| Mouse notches | zooms | unchanged |
| Scrolling outside the picture | — | page scrolls |

`npm run build` (tsc + vite) passes.

Known limit: if a scroll gesture starts on the page and the photo slides under the pointer mid-gesture, Firefox keeps scrolling the page for about 1.5 s. Firefox does this ("wheel transactions") and a page can't override it.

